    icon: '💡',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your cards spread out! If you are holding the Old Maid, try to keep your face neutral. If the player drawing from you sees you smiling or looking nervous when they touch a certain card, they will avoid it. Conversely, if you want them to pick it, try to hide it slightly higher or lower in your hand so it 'sticks out' naturally.\n\nThe 'Card Shuffle': When it's your turn to have a card drawn, shuffle your hand behind your back or under the table. This prevents the drawing player from tracking where you moved the Old Maid from the previous round.\n\nBluff-Targeting: If you have two cards and one is the Old Maid, you can try to trick the opponent by holding the 'safe' card slightly forward. Many children reflexively pick the 'easiest' card to grab. If you know an opponent uses this habit, place the Old Maid in the prominent position.",
    Player: "Keep your cards spread out! If you are holding the Old Maid, try to keep your face neutral. If the player drawing from you sees you smiling or looking nervous when they touch a certain card, they will avoid it. Conversely, if you want them to pick it, try to hide it slightly higher or lower in your hand so it 'sticks out' naturally.\n\nThe 'Card Shuffle': When it's your turn to have a card drawn, shuffle your hand behind your back or under the table. This prevents the drawing player from tracking where you moved the Old Maid from the previous round.\n\nBluff-Targeting: If you have two cards and one is the Old Maid, you can try to trick the opponent by holding the 'safe' card slightly forward. Many children reflexively pick the 'easiest' card to grab. If you know an opponent uses this habit, place the Old Maid in the prominent position.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
    riskTolerance: 0.5,
    bluffFrequency: 0.3,
